# ScreenModes' messages, in TAIRiX Bridge's own words.
BadModeFile:Line %0 of %1 cannot be read as part of a monitor definition
ModeFileTooLarge:%0 is too large to be a monitor definition
NoMonitorFile:No monitor definition file is loaded
BadInfoReason:ScreenModes_ReadInfo has no such reason
BadAudioReason:ScreenModes_EnumerateAudioFormats has no such reason
ModeSizeDisagrees:The mode ending on line %0 of %1 is not the size its timings show
ModeFileEnds:%1 ends inside a mode
ModeNumberLarge:The number on line %0 of %1 is too large
ModeLineTrails:Line %0 of %1 has more on it than it can take
ModeNumberExpected:Line %0 of %1 needs a number
ModeKeyRepeated:Line %0 of %1 gives its mode something it already has
ModeUnnamed:The mode ending on line %0 of %1 has no name
ModeIncomplete:The mode ending on line %0 of %1 lacks its pixel rate, a timing or its syncs
ModeKeyUnknown:Line %0 of %1 gives a mode something no mode has
ModeKeyMisplaced:Line %0 of %1 cannot be inside a mode
ModeFileFormat:%1 is a monitor definition in a format that cannot be read
MonitorTitleBlank:The monitor title on line %0 of %1 is blank
ModeFileEmpty:%1 defines no modes
ModeNoSize:The mode ending on line %0 of %1 has no size or no pixel rate
